      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofpecatonica.com/community/about-us/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Galena and Chicago Union Railroad reached Pecatonica in 1853, linking it to Chicago and Freeport.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pecatonica%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "An electric interurban line ran from Rockford through Pecatonica to Freeport starting in 1902, ending in 1930.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pecatonica%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pecatonica’s elementary school, built in 1938, served as the village’s high school for many years.",
